responses are anonymous.\n58-\n59-  > **Wording rationale (not shown to participants).** This instruction is grounded\n60-  > in the subjective-randomness literature, which warns that naming the structural\n61-  > cues under study (run length / \"streakiness\", alternation / \"switching\", H–T\n62-  > balance) coaches participants and confounds the measurement (Nickerson, 2002,\n63-  > *Psychol. Rev.*; Reimers, Donkin & Le Pelley, 2018, *Cognition*). The accepted\n64-  > practice is to define the generating process — a *fair coin*, 50/50,\n65-  > independent flips — but leave the meaning of \"random-looking\" for the\n66-  > participant to supply from their own intuition (Williams & Griffiths, 2013,\n67-  > *JEP:General*, Exp. 3 nested condition; Griffiths, Daniels, Austerweil &\n68-  > Tenenbaum, 2018, *Cognitive Psychology*). The question phrasing \"which … looks\n----\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>Experiment</title>\n    <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/jspsych@7.3.4\"></script>\n    <link\n      href=\"https://unpkg.com/jspsych@7.3.4/css/jspsych.css\"\n      rel=\"stylesheet\"\n    />\n    <script src=\"https://unpkg.com/@jspsych/plugin-html-button-response@1.1.3\"></script>\n    <style>\n      /* Readable prose block for instructions/debrief — constrained width, left\n       aligned, comfortable line height. Without this, text spans the full screen. */\n      .auto-psych-prose {\n        max-width: 620px;\n        margin: 0 auto;\n        text-align: left;\n        line-height: 1.6;\n        font-size: 18px;\n      }\n      .auto-psych-prose p {\n        margin: 0 0 1em;\n      }\n      .auto-psych-pair {\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: center;\n        gap: 64px;\n        margin: 24px 0;\n      }\n      .auto-psych-seq {\n        font-family: monospace;\n        font-size: 28px;\n        letter-spacing: